't work as one — it will amplify a smear/ladder. If you have the paired primer or the amplicon it came from, the partner may be locus-specific and I can help reason about the intended target.\n\nConfidence: high on the Alu identification (exact 20/20 match to the consensus 5' end, recalled from knowledge, not looked up in a database this session); the ~1.1M copy number and ~10–11% genome fraction are standard published figures, also from knowledge.\n\n## ANSWER\n\nIt has no single location. `GTGAGCCACCGCGCCCGGCC` is the reverse complement of `GGCCGGGCGCGGTGGCTCAC`, the Alu consensus 5' terminus — a standard Alu-PCR primer. It matches thousands of Alu elements on all 24 chromosomes (~1.1 million Alu copies genome-wide in GRCh38), so no unique chromosome/coordinate can be assigned. UNABLE to give coordinates by computation: no alignment tool available in this session."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18937,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18937},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4b11326-5a7b-4b90-81a9-db0057d2c90f","uuid":"3b95e099-5304-47c7-a9df-73d41edad274","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:20:02.440Z","request_id":"req_011CghUsn7RRwsSMSZhY18AJ"}
